  "body": "`get_job` reports an operation's parameters nested under its kind (e.g. `{\"pocket\": {\"stepdown\": ...}}`). Agents - local models especially - copy that shape into `edit_operation`, which refuses it. In the local-model benchmark (2026-11-22, v0.25.0) this was the largest single source of refused calls (10-22 per model over 20 tasks), each costing a model round; the in-app AI chat test (q08) showed the same.\n\nProposal (either):\n1. `edit_operation` accepts the nested shape when the outer key matches the operation's kind (and refuses a mismatched kind by name), or\n2. the refusal message includes the exact corrected call (the flattened patch) so the next round succeeds.\n\nOption 1 is preferred: read and write then use one shape.\n\nDone means: an MCP test that takes an operation's parameters from `get_job`, edits one field using that same nested shape, and succeeds (or, for option 2, gets a refusal containing the corrected patch); the camcraft-mcp skill row is updated.\n",
